here are clues and subtle hints  pointing at a type of system that frank  herbert would be partial to throughout  the book series but it's not exactly  cohesive he seems to be partial with  certain anarchist leaning ideologies see  the friman but he never drives the wedge  home and describes any particular system  that he thinks would be best in the way  that let's say ursula k le guin does in  her work specifically the dispossessed  where she's very clear and defining the  anarchist society  in fact this is what kind of  differentiates frank herbert from a lot  of other authors is that frank herbert  wants you to figure it out on your own  he doesn't want to tell you he wants you  to figure it out  and that is the main key when it comes  to the ending of the dune saga  all right so now let's talk about the  ending so chapter house doing which is a  book that not a lot of people have read  even a lot of dune fans have not read  chapter house dune so in chapter house  dune we are in the meat of the benny  jesuit conflict with their rival  sisterhood the honored matres aka the  honored mothers whose name is of course  reminiscent of the bini jesuit reverent  mothers  at the end of the book we see the  conflict more or less resolved  and then the curtain is pulled back so  to speak and we are officially  introduced to two characters  daniel and marty  and they appear as an old man and an old  woman and they've been kind of watching  the events  of the last several books in the dune  saga perhaps it's not really clear  how long they've been around  but they've definitely been watching for  quite some time  and they have  god like technology that's almost  incomprehensible indescribable and they  were intending to use this technology to  capture  certain protagonists and they were going  to take these protagonists they had an  entire planet picked out for them  apparently and they were going to use  this planet to test the abilities  of these protagonists  but daniel and marty aren't able to  because  the characters  escape from them they get out of their  hands the characters are no longer in  their hands  what we're seeing here in my opinion and  some other people have picked up on this  as well  is frank herbert and his wife beverly  inserting themselves into their story  because a lot of people aren't aware of  the fact that the doomed saga is  essentially a collaboration between  frank herbert and his wife  they inserted themselves into this story  and they allowed the characters to get  away from them  as a way of saying to the readers  now you figure it out  because it does seem like more and more  that the dune books were leading up to  the seventh book  this is the answer this is the structure  of existence where human beings can  exist indefinitely in the universe  that's what it seems like the seventh  book was leading up to that's what it  seems like frank herbert was gonna say  but of course frank herbert never  gives it away  he says i want you to think and that  theme of not being told the answer but  having to figure it out yourself is  something that runs its way throughout  the entire dune saga we see it over and  over and over again it's the very reason  that in the fourth book god emperor of  june that lato does not tell siona to  put on her face mask she has to figure  it out herself  she even says you could have warned me  and he responds  and increased your dependency and  there's also that quote in lato's  fantastic message to the benny desert  where he says with words  you can cry out in the chorus  why didn't someone warn me  but i did warn you  i warned you by example frank herbert is  saying here that the dune saga has  already told you everything you need to  know and it is up to you to think for  yourself and figure out the next step  he's not gonna give it to you  the dune saga is all about test  and we brushed this topic a little bit  on alt shift x's podcast which i was on  the other day link in the description  but the dune saga begins with the test  the tests paul atreides test obviously  and it ends with a test  this time it is our turn  the entire dune saga has been the lesson  and now it's time to see if we can  pass the test so that's just one  interpretation i'm not saying that frank  herbert definitely did not intend to  write a seventh book he definitely could  have left behind a bunch of notes for  what he  would have done  but  i also think that frank herbert could  have been giving himself an out here and  saying that if i don't do another book  this could suffice as an ending if you  really really think about it now i'm not  saying that anything on the surface  level is different to how i previously  interpreted it but thematically i think  that this particular thematic  interpretation is very consistent  let me know what you guys think about  this idea if you enjoy my content you  can follow me on twitter subscribe to me  on this channel make sure you hit the  like button thanks so much guys  [Music]  you
 

